    "site_desc": "The Twitchell Wetland site is a 7.4-acre restored wetland on Twitchell Island, that is managed by the California Department of Water Resources (DWR) and the U.S. Geological Survey (USGS). In the fall of 1997, the site was permanently flooded to a depth of approximately 25 cm. The wetland was almost completely covered by cattails and\ntules by the third growing season.  A flux tower equipped to analyze energy, H2O, CO2, and CH4 fluxes was installed on May 17, 2012.",
